 "response": "Ruzapor's budget is now **$3854K**.\n\n**How I worked it out**\n\n1. I counted only Finance Office budget updates. Notes from PMO, Legal, Sales, Engineering, Vendor and similar sources do not change the budget under the policy. Finance Office messages that are not budget changes were also left out, such as reminders, purchase orders and cost-center codes.\n\n2. Many withdrawals have been withdrawn in turn. For each chain I started from the last withdrawal and worked back. A withdrawal that is itself withdrawn has no effect.\n   - #0005 (+$391K) still applies. Its chain is #0008 \u2190 #0013 \u2190 #0014 \u2190 #0020 \u2190 #0142 \u2190 #0241, and resolving it voids #0008.\n   - #0007 (\u2212$447K) is withdrawn. Its chain is #0021 \u2190 #0024 \u2190 #0039 \u2190 #0046 \u2190 #0133 \u2190 #0214, and resolving it leaves #0021 void and #0024 in force.\n   - Two-step chains restore the original update. Examples are #0029 (via #0262), #0037 (via #0277), #0219 (via #0451/#0585/#0854) and #0652 (via #1424).\n   - In all, 123 budget updates end up withdrawn. Every other Finance Office budget update applies once, in order.\n\n3. The starting budget is $2560K from #0001. The remaining increases and decreases add up to a net +$1294K. That gives $2560K + $1294K = $3854K.\n\nI added the figures in a single running pass and did not do a separate second calculation.\n\nANSWER: $3854K",
